OL,3,GNEWSAEngland Cerebral Palsy World Cup
OL,4,Awin 'unbelievable'
OL,5,
OL,6,FOne of the stars of England's triumph
OL,7,Fat the Cerebral Palsy World Cup has
OL,8,Ftold the BBC the win was
OL,9,F"unbelievable".
OL,11,FThe Para Lions, as they are known, beat
OL,12,Fthe hosts the USA 2-1 in extra time in
OL,13,FAtlanta on Saturday night to win the
OL,14,Ftrophy for the first time.
OL,16,FDavid Porcher, from Chinnor, scored the
OL,17,Fwinning goal in the final, whilst
OL,18,FBanbury's Harry Baker proved to be a
OL,19,Fkey player throughout the tournament.
OL,23,APub: 27-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
